A uniform beam AC is attached to a vertical wall at end A. The beam is held horizontal by a rigid bar BD, as shown in Fig. 3.1.

{{figure:figure_3_1.png}}

The beam is of length $0.40\text{ m}$ and weight $W$. An empty bucket of weight $12\text{ N}$ is suspended by a light metal wire from end C. The bar exerts a force on the beam of $33\text{ N}$ at $52^\circ$ to the horizontal. The beam is in equilibrium.
